WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.409
Good morning, Hank, it's... wait. What day is it? Oh, I can just look at my calendar!

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.799
It's Friday, August 26th! Thank you so much!

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:10.500
It's Question Friday, the day that I answer real questions from real Nerdfighters.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.469
Let's get right to it!

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:14.000
Do you ever get frustrated being a Muggle? How do you know I'm a Muggle?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.800
Favourite essay you have ever read?
The Crack-Up by F. Scott Fitzgerald

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.600
Why hasn't my boyfriend kissed me, even though we've been going for almost five months?

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.000
Wait. Going? Going where? Certainly not the first base. Anybody? Huh?

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.800
Base jokes? Is that still a thing?

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.800
Listen up, anonymous young Twitter user. You are a powerful, young woman.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.000
Kissing is not something that happens TO you, it's something that happens WITH you.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.800
So talk to your boyfriend with whom you have been going, lo, these five months and be honest with him.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.300
How goes the TFIOS signing?

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.400
This somewhat under-represents my progress.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.309
I'm at about 35,000, although I am temporarily out of red Sharpies.

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:49.700
I have a long way to go.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.700
How many Sharpies have you gone through so far?

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:56.100
Like about this many. That's gonna take a while to clean up.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.000
Is it too late to pre-order a signed copy?

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.700
No. All pre-orders of The Fault in Our Stars will be signed.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.800
In fact, the whole first printing is being signed.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.000
Which means, all the books that go out to bookstores are being signed, too.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.840
I just don't know how fast they're gonna sell out, so I can only like

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:12.150
absolutely guarantee that the pre-orders will be signed.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.800
But will you sign the ones from Amazon UK? Yes.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.000
But, does it have to pre-ordered from  -- Yeah, no. All pre-orders will be signed.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.600
Can we pre-order the book from somewhere l --
Yes.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.100
England? Yes! Canada? Yes!

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.600
It doesn't matter where you live or where you pre-order it

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:31.500
or whether you are wearing pants at the time of ordering. All pre-orders will be signed!

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:34.570
(Sighs) Let's move on.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:37.770
What Hogwarts house would you be in? Also, what is the capital of Luxembourg?

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:42.200
I'm kind of a Ravenpuff and Luxembourg. Ravenpuff Luxembourg would be a great Pottermore name.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.000
What's your favorite type of hat?
My people-hunting hat.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.630
How much do you love kittens?

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:50.900
I love kittens like thiiiiiiiis much. I'm not a big kitten person.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.400
Bacon or Cake?
Cakon!

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.300
Just curious, what is your opinion of anime and manga? I also love that you actually say manga right.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.700
First, thank you for noticing my excellent pronunciation of manga.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.800
Second, I love anime and manga.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.570
Describe your favourite paradox.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:05.900
Okay, so you want to walk through a doorway,.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:09.480
But before you can walk through that doorway, you have to walk halfway to the door.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:13.400
And before you can do that, you have to walk halfway to the half-way point, etcetera.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.780
Basically, you have to traverse infinity to go anywhere.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.000
I don't see how you're ever going to get through the door.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.270
That's called Zeno's paradox. It's very important to me.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:23.290
Do you have a tumblr? Do I? 
fishingboatproceeds.tumblr.com. Link in the dooblydoo.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:26.000
Can you do Question Tuesday with peanut butter face? Briefly.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.990
What works of yours are you most proud of?

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:31.140
I'm fairly proud of my career as a professional person who puts peanut butter on his face.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:34.300
Hi? Hi! Favourite punctuation mark? Interrobang!

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.430
Elmo or Grover?

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.970
Right, so every morning I wake up with a song in my head, and for years it was always

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:40.900
a wonderful song like by the Mountain Goats or Hank Green or something.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:43.500
But lately, it's been the same song every morning.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.900
Elmo has two ducks. Quack. Quack.
Two birds of a ... ahh! Grover.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:51.800
How do you feel about Scotland's national animal? Oh, you mean the bagpipes? I love bagpipes!

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:53.900
What do you mean it's not an animal?
Sure, it's an animal.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.700
It responds to stimulus. It can reproduce.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:00.860
It can't? What are all those, like, holes and pointy things for then?

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:05.500
Googling Scotland's national ani--
Unicorns?! I hate them!

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:09.700
Does Sarah have any input into your writing process? Have any of her ideas ever made it into your stories?

00:03:09.769 --> 00:03:13.030
Yeah, tons of stuff. From "Imagining the future is a kind of nostalgia,"

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:15.500
in "Looking for Alaska," to all the pranks in "Paper Towns," and

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.400
she contributed hugely to "The Fault in Our Stars."

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.440
What was the original title of "Looking for Alaska"?

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.300
I had lots of titles: "Misremembering Alaska," "The Great Perhaps."

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.400
For a long time I wanted to call it,  
"Warm Malt Liquour: A Novel"

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.590
I was sorted as a Hufflepuff in Pottermore. Can you console me?

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:32.700
Console you? That you're joining the house of Helga Hufflepuff and Tonks?

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.080
I'm not gonna console you. I'll congratulate you!

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:39.450
Did you ever own a diary? Yeah, I maintained one periodically from 1984 to 1988.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:44.000
It contains such memorable entries as, "Today was a good day. My brother got sick."

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.660
Hank, I'll see you on Monday.

